            <div xml:id="d557">

                <pb facs="0936" n="866" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg866"/>

                <head>No. 558.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Davis to Mr. Wallace.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-07-10"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 10,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 100.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * Your dispatch No. 234, of June 18,
                    reporting the particulars of the flagrant attempt upon the lives of the Rev. Mr.
                    Knapp and Dr. G. C. Reynolds, by Koords, near Bitlis, has been received.</p>
                <p>Your action in the premises is approved, and it is trusted that the offenders
                    will be secured and properly punished. You will convey the Department’s thanks
                    to Mr. Wyndham, Her Majesty’s representative at Constantinople, for his
                    courteous assistance through the British consul at Erzroom in the matter of the
                    complaint of the assaulted gentlemen.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN DAVIS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
